    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Renaissance brought humanism, printing, and golden-age polyphony — Palestrina, Josquin, Byrd."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "polyphony",
      "title": "Polyphony",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Independent vocal lines woven in imitative counterpoint. Mass settings and madrigals. Consonance rules refined; dissonance on weak beats."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "instruments",
      "title": "Instruments",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Lute flourished; viol consort; early keyboard. Dance music published in collections (Attaignant, Praetorius)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "reformation-impact",
      "title": "Reformation impact",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Lutheran chorales and Anglican hymnody shaped congregational singing — ancestors of folk hymn tradition."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
